ts=2026-09-09T10:49:40.213Z action=deleted original_ts=2026-09-08T14:24:03.785Z type=preference scope=preferences content="Hugo has an OpenCode Go subscription (providerID \"opencode-go\") with favorite models: qwen3.8-flash, glm-5.3, gpt-5.6-luna. He prefers using this sub for LLM calls in his apps instead of the free Google Gemini API endpoint." reason="Updated to: Hugo CANCELLED his OpenCode Go subscription (2026-09-09) and now uses the free tier for LLM calls in his apps (originally the free Google Gemini API endpoint in ai-pulse; Zen's free models remain an option via the opt-in opencode provider). The ai-pulse opencode provider code stays as opt-in infrastructure (default LLM_PROVIDER=disabled)." tags=opencode,llm,subscription
ts=2026-09-09T10:49:41.877Z action=deleted original_ts=2026-09-09T09:55:12.234Z type=context scope=ai-pulse content="ai-pulse Epic 3 (dendievel.me design pass) done, stacked PR #21 (base epic/2-config-packs/PR #20). style.css only: accent indigo→green #20e467 (dark) / #15a04a (light warm-paper #f3f0e7), blinking green caret via CSS ::after on .logo h1 + .loading-title (survives __PULSE_NAME_HTML__ injection), nav pills 999px+lift, headings letter-spacing -0.01em. Terminal theme kept amber deliberately. Full stack: #19 opencode provider ← #20 config-packs ← #21 design. All 279 tests green." reason="Updated to: ai-pulse Epic 3 (dendievel.me design pass) reworked per user feedback into a faithful port: light paper theme DEFAULT with exact site palette (paper #ebe8df/#f3f0e7/#e2dfd5, ink #0a0a0a/#2a2a28/#6a6a64/#b6b3aa, links green-deep #15a04a, caret green #20e467), dark theme = site terminal island (#0a0d10/#131418/#e8e6df/#8a8f98, green #20e467), panel green left-bar hover signature, pills per site. User rejected the first iteration (dark-first green swap) — he wants it to look like his website: light by default, exact colors. Amber terminal theme kept. PR #21 updated. Testing via tailscale serve: https://hugos-vm.tail61523.ts.net/ (3200) + :8443 (mac-apps 3201) on the VM." issue=#21 tags=epic3,design,pr-open,stacked,done
ts=2026-09-09T11:06:04.949Z action=deleted original_ts=2026-09-09T10:49:41.877Z type=context scope=ai-pulse content="ai-pulse Epic 3 (dendievel.me design pass) reworked per user feedback into a faithful port: light paper theme DEFAULT with exact site palette (paper #ebe8df/#f3f0e7/#e2dfd5, ink #0a0a0a/#2a2a28/#6a6a64/#b6b3aa, links green-deep #15a04a, caret green #20e467), dark theme = site terminal island (#0a0d10/#131418/#e8e6df/#8a8f98, green #20e467), panel green left-bar hover signature, pills per site. User rejected the first iteration (dark-first green swap) — he wants it to look like his website: light by default, exact colors. Amber terminal theme kept. PR #21 updated. Testing via tailscale serve: https://hugos-vm.tail61523.ts.net/ (3200) + :8443 (mac-apps 3201) on the VM." reason="Updated to: ai-pulse Epic 3 design: TWO user rejections shaped it. 1st: green-on-dark token swap (\"not looking like my website\"). 2nd: exact-colors light port still read as Jarvis HUD (\"doesn't look like my site\") — his site's character is editorial lowercase, mono accents, monochrome restraint. Final approach (fb9a470): typography/voice port, not just colors — lowercase black wordmark + caret, mono green panel titles (site h3 style), no panel header bars, monochrome tag chips replaced rainbow inline-styled chips (edited app.js newsItemHtml), stat labels mono lowercase, pills mono lowercase, orb removed from loading. Lesson: when Hugo says \"make it look like my site\" he means the TYPOGRAPHY and restraint, not the palette swap." issue=#21 tags=epic3,design,rework,user-feedback
